    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bracketed\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen using mini.bracketed, it doesn't respect user's diagnostics config on jump. E.g using this example from the docs https://neovim.io/doc/user/diagnostic/#diagnostic-on-jump-example\n\n```lua\n  --- @param diagnostic? vim.Diagnostic\n  --- @param bufnr integer\n  local function on_jump(diagnostic, bufnr)\n    if not diagnostic then return end\n\n    vim.diagnostic.show(\n      diagnostic.namespace,\n      bufnr,\n      { diagnostic },\n      { virtual_lines = { current_line = true }, virtual_text = false }\n    )\n  end\n\n  vim.diagnostic.config({ jump = { on_jump = on_jump } })\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\"})\nrequire(\"mini.bracketed\").setup()\n\n--- @param diagnostic? vim.Diagnostic\n--- @param bufnr integer\nlocal function on_jump(diagnostic, bufnr)\n    if not diagnostic then return end\n\n    vim.diagnostic.show(\n        diagnostic.namespace,\n        bufnr,\n        { diagnostic },\n        { virtual_lines = { current_line = true }, virtual_text = false }\n    )\nend\n\nvim.diagnostic.config({ jump = { on_jump = on_jump } })\nvim.lsp.enable('lua_ls')\nvim.lsp.config['lua_ls'] = {\n    -- Command and arguments to start the server.\n    cmd = { 'lua-language-server' },\n    -- Filetypes to automatically attach to.\n    filetypes = { 'lua' },\n    -- Sets the \"workspace\" to the directory where any of these files is found.\n    -- Files that share a root directory will reuse the LSP server connection.\n    -- Nested lists indicate equal priority, see |vim.lsp.Config|.\n    root_markers = { { '.luarc.json', '.luarc.jsonc' }, '.git' },\n    -- Specific settings to send to the server. The schema is server-defined.\n    -- Example: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LuaLS/vscode-lua/master/setting/schema.json\n    settings = {\n        Lua = {\n            runtime = {\n                version = 'LuaJIT',\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n4. Open nvim in a folder where the `lua_ls` server starts. Modify a file to get LSP diagnostics (easiest is to create a syntax error). Jump with `]d` and get a floating window for diagnostics instead of virtual lines.\n\n### Workaround\n\nYou can disable mini.bracketed diagnostics with:\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"mini.bracketed\").setup({\n    diagnostic = { suffix = \"\", options = {} },\n})\n```\n\nAnd now you get the correct behavior. \n\n<details><summary>What to do after reporting an issue</summary>\n\nAfter reporting the issue, it is safe (and even recommended for cleaner possible future bug reports) to remove 'nvim-repro' config from the system:\n- Delete config directory ('~/.config/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete data directory ('~/.local/share/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete state directory ('~/.local/state/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n\n</details>\n",
